--- `eigen[a]` answers the real parts and the imaginary parts of a's
--- eigenvalues, a vector each of a's size: its row had declared the second
--- a matrix, so an imaginary part read by position stopped as a fault of
--- Crow's shape rules, and `imag[ev]` had no rank to index (Rosetta Code,
--- Jury stability criterion).
use math

m = [[2.0, 1.0], [1.0, 3.0]]
ev = eigen[m]
log[ev[0][1] + 1.0]
log[ev[1][1] + 1.0]
im = imag[ev]
log[im[0], len[im]]
log[abs[ev[1][0]] lt 0.5]
r = [[0.0, -1.0], [1.0, 0.0]]
spin = eigen[r]
log[spin[0][0], abs[spin[1][0]]]
